      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T14:03:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m of two minds about the best place to store this.\n\nFiniteness is a property of the geometry/points, so it seems to naturally belong to `SkPathData`.  It takes work to track state in `SkPath` and to ensure we don\u0027t end up with different paths disagreeing about the same pathdata being finite.\n\nOTOH we have that friction where we want to communicate transform failure with a non-finite `Empty` path data, but that\u0027s normally a singleton.  Maybe it wouldn\u0027t be too bad to add another `EmptyNonFinite` factory backed by a separate singleton?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1953,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 1953,
        "endChar": 31
      },
